From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:09:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: report the bytes of the heaps it made resident

A host that budgets the GPU memory of its process reads two figures:
Metal's allocation counter, which holds every heap from its creation
and the IOSurfaces of presentation and decoding, and the graphics
ledger, which holds the resident heaps and the driver's command
storage. Each holds memory the other does not, and taking the larger
of the two misses the smaller of the IOSurfaces and the command
storage: about 39 MiB of drawables on an iPad mini 6 at Retina
scale.

kk_resident_heap_bytes() reports the heaps both figures hold, so the
host can add the two and subtract it once. A pooled device makes each
heap resident when it makes it. The heap enters the count as the
residency request is made, while the reservation that covers it is
still held, and leaves it before Metal drops it. The ledger climbs
while the pages become resident, so a heap that entered the count only
after the request returned was counted by Metal, by its reservation and
by the pages that had arrived, up to twice its size over for as long as
the request took (about 100 ms for 128 MiB); the pages that arrive are
now subtracted as they come, and the heap is over-counted by at most
its size, never under-counted. A heap whose residency could not be
requested leaves the count again and waits for the next submission, so
it can only be counted twice, never not at all.
mtl_heap_make_resident() now says whether it made the request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
